---
const steps = [
  {
    actor: "Sending device",
    title: "Verify access",
    body: "Check signed access manifests, referenced group policies, identity pins, and remembered checkpoints.",
  },
  {
    actor: "Sending device",
    title: "Encrypt & wrap",
    body: "Encrypt content. Wrap content keys under container keys, and container keys for the verified recipients.",
  },
  {
    actor: "Sync service",
    title: "Validate & store",
    body: "Enforce write authorization and signed commitments. Store ciphertext and wrapped keys for delivery.",
  },
  {
    actor: "Receiving device",
    title: "Verify & decrypt",
    body: "Verify the signed records and access path, unwrap the keys, and decrypt content locally.",
  },
];
---

<figure class="security-figure" aria-labelledby="sharing-caption">
  <ol class="security-sharing-flow" role="list">
    {steps.map((step, index) => (
      <li class:list={["security-sharing-step", { "security-sharing-step--service": index === 2 }]}>
        <span class="security-eyebrow">{step.actor}</span>
        <span class="security-sharing-number" aria-hidden="true">0{index + 1}</span>
        <h3>{step.title}</h3>
        <p>{step.body}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <div class="security-verification-note">
    <strong>Verification is a gate.</strong>{" "}
    Invalid required signatures, policy chains, or checkpoint comparisons stop the
    affected operation. Server-provided recipient lists alone do not authorize sharing.
  </div>
  <figcaption id="sharing-caption">
    <span class="security-figure-label">Figure 02</span>{" "}
    A simplified shared-content flow. The service checks writes;
    receiving clients independently verify the records they use.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
